# ===========================================================================
# v1.0.59 -- THE FIRST CUT WITH A REAL DAEMON REBUILD SINCE v1.0.53
# ===========================================================================
# v1.0.58's cut.env said, in terms: "DAEMON_COMMIT -- DELIBERATELY NOT
# ADVANCED ... THIS CUT REBUILDS NO DAEMON", and pinned c6fc48c0 across
# v1.0.54 through v1.0.58 because every fix in that window was install.sh.
#
# That is no longer true and the pin CANNOT be reused. oa main moved to
# bc63c445 when #370 landed (#854(i): every registered pwg_* tool is named in
# BOTH prompt branches -- the shipped path takes the COMPACT branch, where the
# interest vocabulary was simply absent). A daemon-side change with no daemon
# rebuild is the "merged is not delivered" failure this estate keeps paying
# for, so v1.0.59 carries a real one: hub-v0.4.70 -> 766ec49a.
#
# ORDER OF PROOF, and it was done in this order deliberately:
#   1. oa Quality Gate on bc63c445 read from the API: completed/success.
#   2. main HEAD == bc63c445 -- the tag names the tree that went green, not a
#      later one. A green gate on a DIFFERENT tree is not evidence about this
#      one, which is the whole of #559's lesson.
#   3. hub-v0.4.70 did not already exist.
#   4. Tag pushed, then the TRIGGER CONFIRMED FIRED by reading the run:
#      "Build macOS assistant binary | push | hub-v0.4.70". A tag that does not
#      start a build is a tag, not a ship.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS CUT HAS NO WALK RECORD WHEN IT IS MADE. THAT IS CORRECT, NOT A GAP.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# walks/v1.0.59.tsv does not exist yet, so verify_walk_record.sh returns rc=2 --
# absence, correctly NOT conflated with badness -- PROMOTE=0, the release stays
# a prerelease, and ostler.ai/install.dmg keeps resolving to its current
# target. The sequence is cut -> walk -> record -> only then promote.
#
# ⚠️ PUT THE DMG IN THE WALKED ACCOUNT'S ~/Downloads. post_walk_qa.sh looks
# only in $HOME/Downloads, $HOME/Desktop and $HOME of the account it walks
# as, and on a CLEAN record the gate then REQUIRES artefact_sha256_source to
# read measured(...). A clean walk whose DMG sits elsewhere yields PROMOTE=0
# for a reason that reads as "no walk evidence" rather than "wrong folder".
#
# 🎩 WALK SUBJECT: the wiped Mini16, 192.168.1.233. macOS 26.5.2, arm64,
# 16 GB, ONE user, no Homebrew, no Docker, no Ollama -- measured, and the first
# genuinely uncontaminated subject we have had. The walk-away install must be
# started AT THE MACHINE: an SSH install is not the thing under test.

CUT_VERSION=1.0.60
DAEMON_COMMIT=bc63c445
# 🔴 REPINNED 2026-09-02. THE PREVIOUS PIN WAS UNRESOLVABLE ON CI, AND IT
# PASSED LOCALLY, WHICH IS THE WHOLE LESSON. 203e19e4 was the head of a
# feature branch that was SQUASH-merged and deleted. A squash writes a NEW
# commit, so the branch's own commits become unreachable from every ref --
# and `actions/checkout` with fetch-depth: 0 fetches ALL REACHABLE history,
# not all objects. CI therefore had no such commit and the gate correctly
# returned CANNOT-RUN rather than pretending to agree.
#
# ⚠️ IT RESOLVED EVERYWHERE I LOOKED FIRST, WHICH IS WHY IT SURVIVED. My
# clone still had the object because the branch had been checked out here,
# and `gh api .../commits/203e19e4` ALSO returns it, because GitHub keeps
# unreachable objects addressable over the API. Two instruments agreed and
# both were measuring something CI does not have. The discriminator is
# `git merge-base --is-ancestor <pin> origin/main`, which answers NO.
#
# THE PIN MUST NAME A COMMIT REACHABLE FROM main. This one is main's head at
# the time of writing, and the gate is not weakened by that: it compares
# install.sh BLOBS, and 00440f72's blob is 8a2c094e -- byte-identical to
# 203e19e4's. Nothing about the tree being cut changed; only the name used
# to reach it did.
CM051=bfc418e23dc5e79a30e18912e906c58b0bd1966b

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.60, opened by scripts/new_cut.sh from v1.0.59.
#
# WHY THESE PINS:
#   v1.0.60 ships the B2 spoken-feed honesty fix (a removed Transcripts 
#   folder no longer reports the fresh-Mac cause), the B3b 
#   extension-credential mint, and A2's G-block source-status artefact with 
#   /api/v1/sources. DAEMON PIN HELD at bc63c445 (hub-v0.4.70) deliberately: 
#   every change in this window is CM051 install.sh or the VENDORED Doctor, 
#   so there is no daemon-side commit to carry and rebuilding would spend a 
#   version for nothing. CM051 pin is main head bfc418e2, proved reachable by 
#   git merge-base --is-ancestor with 203e19e4 as the discriminating control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
